  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Commerce obligated $147M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Commerce recorded 580 awards with an average award size of $254K, and obligations fell 97.1% year over year. The FY27 total is partial, fiscal year to date, while prior full-year obligations were $4.1B in FY22, $5B in FY23, $5.2B in FY24, $4.2B in FY25, and $5.1B in FY26. Other Computer Related Services and Computer Systems Design Services account for the largest shares of FY2027 to date obligations at $80.9M and $39.3M respectively, followed by a mix of engineering, R&D, information services, and facilities-related categories. GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. and ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC are the top vendors in FY2027 to date with $61M and $12.6M in obligations respectively, and the rest of the top ten vendors range from $9.7M down to $2.6M. This snapshot reflects a much smaller fiscal-year-to-date spend compared with prior full-year totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How much has Commerce obligated so far in FY2027?",
        "body": "The Department of Commerce obligated $147M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Commerce recorded 580 awards with an average award size of $254K. Obligations fell 97.1% year over year. The FY27 total is a partial, fiscal year to date figure."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What did Commerce buy and who got the work?",
        "body": "Other Computer Related Services received $80.9M and Computer Systems Design Services received $39.3M in FY2027 to date. GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. received $61M and ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC received $12.6M, with other top vendors ranging from $9.7M to $2.6M. The category mix includes engineering, R&D, information services, facilities support, and security services."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Commerce spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Commerce obligated $147M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Commerce recorded 580 awards and an average award size of $254K, and obligations fell 97.1% year over year. The FY27 total is a partial, fiscal year to date figure; prior full-year obligations were $4.1B in FY22, $5B in FY23, $5.2B in FY24, $4.2B in FY25, and $5.1B in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Commerce buy?",
      "a": "Commerce buys a mix of IT, professional services, engineering, and facilities support. Other Computer Related Services received $80.9M and Computer Systems Design Services received $39.3M in FY2027 to date, with additional spending across engineering, R&D, information services, computer facilities management, and facilities support."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Commerce's largest contractors?",
      "a": "GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. and ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC are Commerce's largest contractors in FY2027 to date, receiving $61M and $12.6M respectively. Other top contractors in FY2027 to date include EXECUTIVE INFORMATION SYSTEMS, L.L.C. at $9.7M, HALVIK LLC at $9.6M, and BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC at $9.2M, with the rest of the top ten ranging from $7.8M to $2.6M."
